-- title:
--   Existence of a level-n Mumford gluing datum
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$, a commutative domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible element $\pi\in\mathcal O$ whose residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements, and a field $K_0$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra and a fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $g_1\in GL_2(K_0)$ be the diagonal matrix $\mathrm{diag}(\pi,1)$ and let $N$ be a subgroup of $PGL(2,K_0)$ subject to two conditions on its action on the Bruhat–Tits graph $\mathcal T=$ `BruhatTits.tree` $\mathcal O\,K_0$ (whose vertices are homothety classes of full $\mathcal O$-lattices in $K_0^2$, adjacency being generated by `AdjacentLattice`): first, `IsSchottky`, i.e. every vertex stabiliser in $N$ is trivial, no element of $N$ carries a dart to its reverse, and the sets of $N$-orbits of vertices and of darts are finite; second, $N$ lies in `typePreserving`, i.e. every element of $N$ preserves the parity of the graph distance to the standard vertex. For every $n\in\mathbb N$ the conclusion asserts that the type `MumfordGlueLevel` $\mathcal O\,\pi\,K_0\,r\,g_1\,N\,n$ is nonempty: there exists a scheme $Z$ flat and separated over $\mathrm{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$, together with edge charts $\zeta_h$ indexed by $h\in GL_2(K_0)$, which are open immersions of $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the edge chart ring `chartERing` $\mathcal O\,\pi\,r$ modulo $\pi^{n+1}$ over $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$, finitely many of which cover $Z$ and which satisfy $\zeta_{gh}=\zeta_h$ whenever the class of $g$ lies in $N$; an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\iota$ from the edge chart ring mod $\pi^{n+1}$ to the vertex chart ring `chartVRing` $\mathcal O\,r$ mod $\pi^{n+1}$ sending $\xi\mapsto\zeta$, with $\iota(\eta)\cdot\zeta=\pi$ and exhibiting the target as the localisation away from $\xi$; transports $\tau_g$, $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphisms of the vertex chart ring mod $\pi^{n+1}$ characterised, for $g$ fixing the standard vertex, by a condition on the lines that a `DeligneDatum` over an $\mathcal O$-algebra attaches to the standard lattice and to $g_1$ applied to it; and the remaining gluing, incidence and transport laws of `MumfordGlueLevel`, summarised here.
--
--   This is one level, modulo $\pi^{n+1}$, of Mumford's gluing construction of the quotient of the formal upper half plane by a type-preserving Schottky subgroup of $PGL_2(K_0)$, in the form used for the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation. It is the inductive input to [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueCore_of_isSchottky`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalOmega.nonempty_mumfordGlueCore_of_isSchottky), which assembles the levels into a formal scheme over $\mathcal O$.
